# Line endings.
#
# The repository stores LF, and every tool in the gate expects LF: phpcs PSR-12
# fails a file outright on "End of line character is invalid", and Prettier
# rewrites CRLF on sight. Windows checkouts, however, get CRLF from
# core.autocrlf=true — so `composer lint` failed on 34 files nobody had edited,
# and `git checkout` kept undoing what Prettier had just fixed.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf, so this holds regardless of each developer's
# global git config, and no per-machine setup is required.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Nothing here needs CRLF today (no .bat/.cmd exist). If one is ever added it
# must opt out, because cmd.exe mis-parses LF-terminated batch files:
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: excluded explicitly rather than relying on content detection,
# so a stray text-looking header can never get "normalised" into corruption.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.db binary
